      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1775197043032,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Now you can monitor whatever metric you want to,based on the above\nsteps in the cloudwatch dashboard",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Now you can monitor whatever metric you want to,based on the above\nsteps in the cloudwatch dashboard",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "D8SbRfiDyC1jRpp8UwVpk",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 368.3740918117001,
      "y": 622.9403978874856,
      "width": 1098.599365234375,
      "height": 200,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b41",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 193941791,
      "version": 207,
      "versionNonce": 1303872177,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1775197163963,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "CloudWatch vs. CloudTrail\nThese two services are often confused, but they serve very different purposes.\n\nFeature        Amazon CloudWatch                                 AWS CloudTrail\nFocus          Performance & Monitoring.                         Auditing & Compliance.\nAnswers       \"Is my server slow?\" \"Is my CPU high?\"          \"Who deleted the database?\" \"When did they do it?\"\nData Type    Metrics & Logs.                                      API Activity History.\nExample        90% CPU Utilization.                               User Alice called TerminateInstance at 2:00 PM.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "CloudWatch vs. CloudTrail\nThese two services are often confused, but they serve very different purposes.\n\nFeature        Amazon CloudWatch                                 AWS CloudTrail\nFocus          Performance & Monitoring.                         Auditing & Compliance.\nAnswers       \"Is my server slow?\" \"Is my CPU high?\"          \"Who deleted the database?\" \"When did they do it?\"\nData Type    Metrics & Logs.                                      API Activity History.\nExample        90% CPU Utilization.                               User Alice called TerminateInstance at 2:00 PM.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
